  "findings": [
    {
      "level": "CLASS",
      "where": "SKILL.md frontmatter description vs Step 0 / evals 1 and 4",
      "finding": "The description promises a cut unconditionally, but the body's most-weighted rule and half the graded cases require producing NO cut. Two of four evals (1 and 4) are scored on refusing to give a cut, and the description names neither the no-data stop nor the separation gate that produces those refusals. A reader routed by the description alone gets a skill that always answers with a threshold.",
      "quote": "Produces the cut, the precision it holds and the coverage it costs, against a precision target and a coverage floor agreed first. // If there is none, stop at step 1 and say so. ... and state no cut, no coverage and no band."
    },
    {
      "level": "CLASS",
      "where": "SKILL.md Step 0 vs Step 5, Step 7, and assets/threshold-decision-record.md sections 3 and 5",
      "finding": "The no-data path orders delivery of record section 5, whose required fields are the abstained volume per period, capacity against it, and a headroom figure. Step 7 sources that volume 'from step 5', and step 5 cannot run because there is no holdout; the record itself forbids supplying it any other way. So the step the skill weights most demands a number its own rules forbid computing - and eval 1 E2 fails any answer that states a coverage figure in any form, which is what a filled section 5 needs.",
      "quote": "Deliver sections 0, 1 and 5 of the record, name what has to be pulled and who pulls it, and state no cut, no coverage and no band. // Capacity: <n per period> against <n per period> abstained. Headroom: <value>. // If section 0 says NO, this table has no rows - it does not get a range, an estimate, or a band."
